         } ] [--nneett _n_e_t_w_o_r_k_c_o_d_e] [--ttxxtt _t_e_x_t] [_p_b_m_f_i_l_e]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppbbmmttoonnookkiiaa  reads  a PBM image as input and produces a Nokia Smart Mes‐
       saging (hexcode, .ngg, .nol, .npm) file as output.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppbbmmttoonnookkiiaa recognizes the
       following command line options:



       --ffmmtt   Specifies the output format (default is HEX_NOL).



       HHEEXX__NNOOLL
              Nokia Operator Logo as (uploadable) hexcode.  Use option -net to
              specify network code.


       HHEEXX__NNGGGG
              Nokia Group Graphic as (uploadable) hexcode.


       HHEEXX__NNPPMM
              Nokia  Picture Message as (uploadable) hexcode.  Use option --ttxxtt
              to specify an optional text message.


       NNOOLL    Nokia Operator Logo as .nol format.  This  is  editable  by  the
              Group-Graphic Editor from Kessler Wireless Design ( www.kessler-
              design.com ⟨http://www.kessler-design.com⟩ )


       NNGGGG    Nokia Group Graphic as .ngg format.  This  is  editable  by  the
              Group-Graphic Editor from Kessler Wireless Design ( www.kessler-
              design.com ⟨http://www.kessler-design.com⟩ )


       NNPPMM    Nokia Picture Message as .npm format. This is  editable  by  the
              Picture-Message   Editor   from   Kessler   Wireless   Design  (
              www.kessler-design.com ⟨http://www.kessler-design.com⟩ )

              This option was new in Netpbm 10.36 (October 2006).




       --nneett   Specifies the 6 hex-digit operator network code for Operator Lo‐
              gos (Default is 62F210 = D1,Germany).


       --ttxxtt   Specifies  the  text  message for Picture Messages.  The maximum
              size text message allowed by the format is 120 characters.

              Default is no text message.




LLIIMMIITTAATTIIOONNSS
       This program currently accepts all PBM images with up to 255 rows or up
       to  255  columns.  (Valid Nokia Group Graphics or Operator Logos can be
       72 columns by 14 rows and 78 columns by 21 rows;  valid  Nokia  Picture
       Messages  are 72 columns by 28 rows.)  This program generates black and
       white graphics, not animated.


